course: dictionary
lesson: 9124
title: Smoothly: with no bumps or trouble
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Smoothly» is an adverb, so it tells us how something happens. It describes the way an action is done, like moving or going.
explain: It has three main meanings: in an even way with no bumps or sudden stops, without problems, and in a calm, easy way. «The trip went smoothly» means there were no problems. Read the words around it to find which meaning fits.
explain: Use the check: swap in a meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense. A car that moves smoothly has no jerks, a plan that goes smoothly has no trouble, and a speaker who speaks smoothly sounds calm and easy.
fact: «Smoothly» means in an even way, with no bumps or sudden stops.
fact: «Smoothly» can also mean without problems or trouble, as in a plan that goes smoothly.
fact: «Smoothly» can mean in a calm, easy way, as in speaking smoothly.
fact: Things slide smoothly on ice because there is little friction.
fact: Common phrases with this word are «run smoothly», «go smoothly» and «move smoothly».
exercise: «The trip went smoothly.» What does smoothly mean here? | Sadly and slowly | With a loud bump | *Without problems or trouble | Very fast and noisy
exercise: «The car moved smoothly over the road.» What does smoothly suggest? | In a jerky, bumpy way | *Along with no bumps or sudden stops | Very loudly | Backwards in a circle
exercise: Which phrase shows the plan had no problems? | The plan fell off the table | The plan was shouted loudly | The plan stopped with a jolt | *The plan went smoothly
test: «Oil paint dries slowly, so painters can blend it smoothly for days.» What does smoothly mean here? | Upside down | Very quickly and roughly | *In an even way, with no lumps | With a loud noise
test: «Shark skin helps water flow smoothly.» What does smoothly suggest? | Very noisily | *With little resistance and no sudden stops | Full of bumps and splashes | Backwards, against the water
exam: Which sentence uses smoothly to mean calm and easy? | *She answered the questions smoothly and calmly | The bike crashed into the fence | The sky went dark quickly | He ran out of the room shouting
